    <a href="/blog" class="text-gray-500 hover:text-orange-500 text-sm mb-6 block">← Back to Blog</a>
    <div class="mb-8"><div class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">August 6, 2026 · VPS Provider Review · 11 min read</div><h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Scaleway VPS Review 2026: EU Sovereign Cloud from €4.99/mo</h1><p class="text-xl text-gray-400">A French, EU-resident cloud with unlimited-traffic Dedibox VPS across 20+ locations and zero-egress hourly Instances — is it worth it over US budget hosts?</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">What Scaleway Offers in 2026</h2><p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">Scaleway is a French cloud provider owned by the Iliad Group — the same company behind the Free telecom brand. It has spent the last several years positioning itself as the European sovereign-cloud alternative to US hyperscalers: EU data residency, a French operator, and pricing that undercuts the big three. For VPS buyers, the relevant question is how its two compute products stack up.</p><p class="text-gray-300">There are two paths. Dedibox VPS is the monthly-billed, standalone VPS: full root access on shared KVM hardware, unlimited traffic, and 20+ worldwide locations at uniform pricing from €4.99/mo. Public Cloud Instances are the hourly-billed VMs inside the broader Scaleway ecosystem — Paris, Amsterdam, and Warsaw regions, object storage, managed databases, VPC, and zero egress fees. Which one you want depends on whether you need the standalone VPS or the full cloud.</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Dedibox VPS Pricing and the Three Ranges</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm"><thead><tr class="border-b border-gray-700 text-gray-400"><th class="text-left py-3 pr-4">Plan</th><th class="text-left py-3 pr-4">vCPU</th><th class="text-left py-3 pr-4">RAM</th><th class="text-left py-3 pr-4">NVMe</th><th class="text-left py-3 pr-4">Price</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">START-2-XS</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-gray-300">1 vCPU</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">1 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">20 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-orange-400">€4.99/mo</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">PRO-2-XS</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-gray-300">1 vCPU</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">2 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">50 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-orange-400">€7.99/mo</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">PRO-2-M</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-gray-300">4 vCPU</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">8 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">125 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-orange-400">€17.49/mo</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">STORE-2-XS</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-gray-300">1 vCPU</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">2 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">250 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-orange-400">€7.99/mo</td></tr><tr><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-white">STORE-2-M</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-gray-300">4 vCPU</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">8 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4">1024 GB</td><td class="py-3 pr-4 text-orange-400">€32.49/mo</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="text-gray-400 mt-4">Dedibox VPS splits into three ranges. START uses standard CPUs and 20–100 GB NVMe, from €4.99/mo. PRO uses premium CPUs with up to 1 TB NVMe, from €7.99/mo. STORE pairs premium CPUs with high-capacity NVMe (up to 16 TB) and 10 Gbit/s networking, from €7.99/mo. Pricing is uniform worldwide — the same plan costs the same in Paris as in Singapore or São Paulo.</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">The EU Sovereign Angle</h2><p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">Scaleway's clearest differentiator is where it sits. A French operator with core regions in Paris, Amsterdam, and Warsaw, it is positioned as a sovereign-European cloud — a domestic alternative for buyers who are uncomfortable with US-based providers or who have GDPR, data-residency, or public-sector compliance constraints. That is a genuinely different value proposition from the US budget hosts that dominate this market.</p><p class="text-gray-300">For EU-resident production workloads, this matters in a practical way: data stored and processed in EU regions keeps you inside the GDPR data-adequacy framework without extra contractual gymnastics, and the provider itself is subject to EU jurisdiction. If that is a requirement for your project, very few budget-priced clouds can claim the same.</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Bandwidth: Unlimited Traffic and Zero Egress</h2><p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">Bandwidth policy is where Scaleway stands out. Dedibox VPS includes unlimited traffic, with fair-use throttling beyond a certain threshold per plan rather than metered billing. Public Cloud Instances advertise no outbound data-transfer (egress) fees at all. For a bandwidth-heavy workload — media streaming, file distribution, sync, proxies — this removes one of the biggest line items on most hosted bills.</p><p class="text-gray-300">The nuance is the fair-use rule on Dedibox VPS: the unthrottled bandwidth included scales with the plan, and sustained far-above-threshold usage gets capped. That is a reasonable middle ground for honest workloads, but if you expect genuinely massive sustained transfer, confirm the specific threshold for your plan before committing.</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Global Locations at Uniform Pricing</h2><p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">Dedibox VPS is offered in 20+ locations across North America (New York, Dallas, Chicago, Los Angeles, Toronto, Montreal), South America (São Paulo, Buenos Aires, Santiago), Europe (Paris, Frankfurt, London, Amsterdam, Madrid, Stockholm, Zurich), and APAC/MEA (Singapore, Tokyo, Hong Kong, Sydney, Mumbai, Tel Aviv). The uniform-global-pricing policy means you pay the same for a given spec in any of these — handy for teams hosting the same workload for audiences in several regions.</p><p class="text-gray-300">Public Cloud Instances, in contrast, are anchored to three core regions — Paris (FR-PAR), Amsterdam (NL-AMS), and Warsaw (PL-WAW) — which is fewer than US hyperscalers but a solid EU footprint for most workloads. Choose Dedibox VPS for global coverage or Instances for the EU hairpin with the full ecosystem.</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Developer Ecosystem: API, Terraform, VPC</h2><p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">On the Public Cloud side, Scaleway is one of the more developer-friendly European clouds. There is a full API, a CLI, a Terraform provider, S3-compatible object storage, managed databases (PostgreSQL, MySQL, Redis, MongoDB), and VPC/Private Network plus IPAM for private networking. That makes it a credible platform for teams that want infrastructure-as-code rather than a single static VPS.</p><p class="text-gray-300">Dedibox VPS is deliberately simpler and standalone — the documentation is explicit that it is not compatible with the Dedibox dedicated-server ecosystem (RPN, Failover IPs, Dedibackup, RPN-SAN). If you want those add-ons, you buy a Dedibox dedicated server instead. For a pure VPS, the standalone model is actually cleaner.</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Support and Billing</h2><p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">Billing is straightforward: affordable monthly pricing with no hidden fees on Dedibox VPS, and hourly billing on Public Cloud Instances — which is convenient for spin-up-and-tear-down workloads. Support runs through Scaleway's console/ticket system with extensive documentation; it is reliable but not white-glove, and the entry tiers are unmanaged, so you handle the OS, updates, and security.</p><p class="text-gray-300">One thing to note for non-EU buyers: prices are quoted excluding VAT, and VAT may be added at checkout depending on your location. As with any provider, read the exact invoice before committing to a long-running production project.</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Scaleway vs RackNerd and US Budget Hosts</h2><p class="text-gray-300 mb-4"><a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RackNerd</a> remains the cleaner baseline for buyers who want ultra-low-cost annual specials, US datacenter coverage, and no-frills month-to-month pricing. Scaleway wins on European sovereignty, EU data residency, zero-egress Instances, and a richer cloud ecosystem. For an EU-resident production workload with compliance requirements, Scaleway's €4.99/mo Dedibox VPS entry and €7.99/mo PRO range deliver strong value with the peace of mind of EU jurisdiction.</p><p class="text-gray-300">For a throwaway test box or a tiny-budget project with no data-residency needs, a US budget host is still cheaper and simpler. The two are answering different questions; pick based on whether sovereignty and ecosystem matter to you.</p></div>

    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Our Verdict: 4.3/5 for EU-Resident Developers</h2><p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">Scaleway earns 4.3/5 for developers who value European sovereignty and predictable bandwidth pricing. Unlimited-traffic Dedibox VPS from €4.99/mo in 20+ locations and zero-egress hourly Instances in Paris, Amsterdam, and Warsaw make it one of the strongest EU-native clouds in 2026.</p><p class="text-gray-300">The standalone nature of Dedibox VPS (no RPN/Failover/Dedibackup), the premium-CPU upsell on the START range, and unmanaged entry tiers keep it just short of the top tier. Before ordering, decide which product fits — standalone monthly VPS or the full hourly cloud — confirm your location is in stock, and set up external backups for anything irreplaceable.</p></div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-8"><div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-green-400">Who should choose it?</h2><ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300"><li>✅ EU-resident production workloads with GDPR/data-residency needs</li><li>✅ Teams that want a sovereign-European cloud alternative</li><li>✅ Bandwidth-heavy workloads that benefit from unlimited/zero-egress traffic</li><li>✅ Developers using API, CLI, Terraform, or the Public Cloud ecosystem</li><li>✅ Same-server-spec deployments across many global locations</li></ul></div><div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-red-400">Who should skip it?</h2><ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-300"><li>⚠️ Anyone who wants the absolute lowest entry price</li><li>⚠️ Buyers needing Dedibox dedicated add-ons (RPN, Failover, Dedibackup) on a VPS</li><li>⚠️ Teams that need many Asian regions beyond Tokyo/Singapore/Hong Kong</li><li>⚠️ Beginners looking for managed administration on the cheap tiers</li><li>⚠️ Anyone without an independent backup plan</li></ul></div></div>

    <div class="bg-orange-500/10 border border-orange-500/20 rounded-xl p-6"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Compare VPS pricing before you commit</h2><p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Use our <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd comparison link</a> as a low-cost baseline, then match RAM, region, bandwidth, and EU data-residency requirements against Scaleway.</p><a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-block bg-green-600 hover:bg-green-500 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-medium transition">Compare VPS options →</a></div>
